The reason for this restriction is specific and worth stating plainly: an
openly licensed question bank aimed at a certification can be forked, stripped
of its citations and its clean-room provenance, and republished as an exam
braindump. This project's entire claim to legitimacy is that every item is
original, evidence-backed, and traceable to public documentation. That claim
does not survive uncontrolled redistribution.

